<title>USA: Atchison Casting unit wins two new orders.</title>
<headline>Atchison Casting unit wins two new orders.</headline>
<dateline>ATCHISON, Kan. 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atchison Casting Corp said Thursday its Canadian Steel Foundries unit won new orders from companies in Sweden and China.</p>
<p>Atchison said it received a $2.7-million contract from Kvaerner Turbin AB, a turbine-generator equipment maker based in Sweden. The castings are for the Companhia Paranaese de Energia's Salto Caxias hydroelectric power plant in Brazil.</p>
<p>Atchison also received a $500,000 casting order from Dongfang Electric Machinery Company in Sichuan Province, China, for a hydroelectric plant on the Yalong River.</p>
<p>Atchison makes, iron, steel and other castings for a variety of industries. It stock was unchanged Thursday at 17-1/4.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
